export function buildPrompt(s,assetById,scenes){
 const mode=s.generation||'natural';
 const counts=new Map();for(const i of s.items){const a=assetById[i.type],key=`${a.name} (${a.en}), natural ${a.color}`;counts.set(key,(counts.get(key)||0)+1)}
 const palette=[...counts].map(([name,count])=>`- ${name}; approximately ${count} selected stems`).join('\n');
 const freedom={natural:'Reconstruct the arrangement as a skilled florist would in real life. Keep the floral identity, broad gesture, dominant color relationships, asymmetry and breathing space. Freely adjust individual stem curvature, relative spacing, flower-head orientations, overlaps, modest length differences and depth until everything looks organically grown and physically arranged.',creative:'Treat this study as an art-direction moodboard. Keep the chosen botanical families, dominant palette, vessel character and emotional intention. You may substantially reinterpret branch paths, spacing, heights, flower faces, balance and negative space to make a fresh, sophisticated composition. Preserve the quiet ikebana character; do not turn it into a dense commercial bouquet.',faithful:'Stay reasonably close to the broad layout, principal stem directions, scale hierarchy and areas of negative space. Still correct rigid joints, implausible intersections, repeated flower faces and pasted-on proportions. Minor natural changes in curves, depth, spacing and flower orientation are welcome; never trace the collage literally.'};
 return `Create an original, professional photographic ikebana still life inspired by the attached draft.png. The attachment is a rough human-made design study, not a finished artwork to reproduce pixel for pixel.\n\nINTENTION\nTitle: ${s.title||'Untitled'}. Mood: ${s.mood}. ${s.intention}\n\nCREATIVE FREEDOM\n${freedom[mode]}\n\nBOTANICAL PALETTE\n${palette||'Use the visible botanical selection in the reference.'}\nThe listed quantities describe the rough study, not a rigid count of individual blooms. Preserve the selected species and natural color families. Subtle bud and leaf variation is welcome where botanically plausible. When the draft contains pruned areas, keep the resulting openness rather than recreating the erased foliage.\n\nVESSEL & SETTING\n${assetById[s.vessel].name} (${assetById[s.vessel].en}); retain its material and general silhouette. ${scenes[s.scene][2]}. Arrange the stems with a believable common insertion into the vessel. Work in a real three-dimensional space, with front, middle and rear planes, slight asymmetry, gravity and organic tension.\n\nPHOTOGRAPHIC FINISH\nNeutral daylight white balance, accurate botanical pigmentation, restrained saturation with subtle hue variation within petals and leaves, translucent petal edges, fine veins and matte/waxy surface differences. One coherent soft window light from upper left, natural contact shadows and believable depth of field. Elegant gallery-quality botanical still-life photography, calm 1:1 framing and ample negative space.\n\nREINTERPRET, DO NOT TRACE\nDo not copy the collage's cutout edges, flat lighting, exact coordinates, duplicated poses, mechanical straight stems or artificial color cast. Rebuild the living materials from the creative intent. Avoid plastic shine, oversaturation, floating stems, illustration, 3D-render appearance, ornamental clutter, text, borders and watermarks.\n\nPriority: a living, natural arrangement with the author's intent > literal similarity to the draft.`;
}

